From 8da72eeffd26975e714289d5378fc8101539524a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:15:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The assertion this migration calls has to exist
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The replay failed at line 290 of the 09:00 file:

    ERROR: function erp.assert_execute_grants_match_reach() does not exist

It never existed. I wrote the name from memory and then checked it with a
grep that matched the migration doing the asking — the file confirmed
itself. That is the same shape of mistake this repository already refuses
elsewhere: a check that proves nothing because it reads the claim rather
than the catalogue.

The real assertion is erp.assert_invoker_doors_executable(), defined in
20260906020000, which raises CLOVEERP_EXECUTE_GRANTS_DRIFTED and whose own
hint names erp.apply_execute_grants() as the fix. Every other assertion
this file calls was checked for a definition, not a mention.

Replaced rather than edited. The 09:00 file applied nowhere — the replay
died on it — and a branch that adds a file and removes it again leaves no
trace in the diff against its base, so neither 'A migration is written
once' nor the deletion guard has anything to object to, and no history
that ran anywhere is rewritten.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W2VdSJb8Tsz44kPmPhDt4M
---
 ...r_writes_only_what_is_not_already_there.sql} | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 rename supabase/migrations/{20260912090000_a_generator_writes_only_what_is_not_already_there.sql => 20260912093000_a_generator_writes_only_what_is_not_already_there.sql} (92%)

diff --git a/supabase/migrations/20260912090000_a_generator_writes_only_what_is_not_already_there.sql b/supabase/migrations/20260912093000_a_generator_writes_only_what_is_not_already_there.sql
similarity index 92%
rename from supabase/migrations/20260912090000_a_generator_writes_only_what_is_not_already_there.sql
rename to supabase/migrations/20260912093000_a_generator_writes_only_what_is_not_already_there.sql
index 02db3bc..f3e09a6 100644
--- a/supabase/migrations/20260912090000_a_generator_writes_only_what_is_not_already_there.sql
+++ b/supabase/migrations/20260912093000_a_generator_writes_only_what_is_not_already_there.sql
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 -- already held is not re-issued. The end state is identical — which is the
 -- whole point, and is why this needs no new assertion to be trusted:
 -- erp.assert_audit_coverage() reads erp.audit_coverage_report() and
--- erp.assert_execute_grants_match_reach() reads the register, both against the
+-- erp.assert_invoker_doors_executable() reads the catalogue, both against the
 -- catalogue rather than against what a generator claims it did. A generator
 -- that skipped something it should not have fails the same build it always did,
 -- in the same migration.
@@ -38,6 +38,19 @@
 -- worse than no number.
 -- =============================================================================
 
+-- Reissued at 09:30 rather than 09:00. The first version of this file called
+-- erp.assert_execute_grants_match_reach(), which does not exist and never did —
+-- the name was written from memory and then "verified" by a grep that matched
+-- the file doing the asking. The replay failed on it at line 290. The real
+-- assertion is erp.assert_invoker_doors_executable(), which raises
+-- CLOVEERP_EXECUTE_GRANTS_DRIFTED and whose own hint names
+-- erp.apply_execute_grants() as the fix.
+--
+-- Replaced rather than edited: the 09:00 file never applied anywhere, and a
+-- branch that adds a file and removes it again leaves no trace in the diff
+-- against its base, so neither "A migration is written once" nor the deletion
+-- guard has anything to object to. Nothing that ran has been rewritten.
+
 set lock_timeout = '30s';
 
 -- Audit coverage --------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -287,7 +300,7 @@ select erp.apply_execute_grants();
 
 select erp.assert_isolation();
 select erp.assert_audit_coverage();
-select erp.assert_execute_grants_match_reach();
+select erp.assert_invoker_doors_executable();
 select erp.assert_no_public_execute();
 select erp.assert_no_caller_reachable_internals();
 select erp.assert_public_api_safe();
